    "kind": "canonical-localization-generations",
    "mount_composition": "Three separate generations meet the runtime's fixed layout under FS2_ARTIFACT_ROOT. The checkpoint is bound as a single entry at mosaic/boltz/boltz2_conf.ckpt and its sibling molecule directory at mosaic/boltz/mols, so the intermediate mosaic/boltz directory is a kubelet-created mount point rather than a mount, and neither bind nests inside the other's read-only mount.",
    "read_only": true
  },
  "claim": "The immutable adapter-v5 digest ran the full single-shard binder-design workflow and its aggregate on real H100 capacity with every model byte supplied by an accepted content-addressed localization generation, each admitted by its own in-generation marker inside the consuming pod. This closes the lock's transitional-task-scoped artifact delivery: the earlier semantic run read a copy on a shared qualification claim.",
  "cleanup": {
    "autoscaled_node": "The h100-1x node the first attempt triggered was left to the cluster autoscaler to reclaim rather than deleted by hand.",
    "removed_after_collection": [
      "pod/fs2-mosaic-canon-reader",
      "pod/fs2-mosaic-canon-export",
      "job/fs2-mosaic-identity-r20260904b",
      "job/fs2-mosaic-mols-r20260904",
      "job/fs2-localize-stage-r20260904m1",
      "configmap/fs2-mosaic-compute",
