      "configmap/fs2-mosaic-loc-verifier",
      "configmap/fs2-mosaic-canon-inputs",
      "configmap/fs2-loc-verifier-r20260904m1"
    ],
    "retained": "The two published generations and their in-generation markers are the deliverable and stay on the public plane. The 4.2 GiB of verified upstream downloads under downloads/mosaic-localization are removed; the generations no longer need them."
  },
  "findings": [
    {
      "detail": "The first attempt was admitted by Kueue onto the inference-h100-1x flavor, which has nominal quota for two GPUs but no Ready node. The pod was injected with that flavor's node labels, could not schedule, and triggered a 0->1 scale-up of a node group. Pinning accelerator.fs2.nebius/pool-id=h100-reserved-8x makes Kueue choose the flavor whose nodes exist. The job was deleted as soon as this was observed.",
      "id": "kueue-flavor-h100-1x-has-quota-but-no-ready-node"
    },
    {
      "detail": "With pod fsGroup 10001 and the shared run claim mounted at its root, the kubelet chowned the whole claim before any container started: 92 s and 51,679 files, delaying marker admission and the GPU stage. Setting fsGroupChangePolicy OnRootMismatch and mounting a per-run subdirectory removed the delay entirely; the successful attempt reached Running in 46 s.",
      "id": "recursive-volume-ownership-on-the-run-claim"
    },
    {
      "detail": "The plan derives the shard output path from the request digest, so a re-run against the same claim collides with the historical run. The runtime refuses it with exist_ok=False, which is correct behaviour and not a defect; a per-run subdirectory is the fix. The first attempt failed this way after completing all 20 optimizer steps on GPU.",
      "id": "runtime-refuses-a-dirty-shard-output-directory"
    }
  ],
